module phosphorylationDetection
module cellViabilityDetection

manifest NIH3T3_Cells
manifest SeumFreeMedia
manifest StarvedMedia
manifest CultureMedia
manifest PluronicF68
manifest PDGFBB_Ligand
manifest Paraformaldehyde
manifest WashBuffer1
manifest WashBuffer2
manifest Tween20
manifest BlockingSolution
manifest PrimaryAntibody_PDGFR
manifest PrimaryAntibody_pPDGFR_Y857
manifest PrimaryAntibody_pPDGFR_Y1021
manifest PrimaryAntibody_Akt
manifest PrimaryAntibody_pAkt_S473
manifest SecondaryAntibody_AlexaFluor647
manifest SecondaryAntibody_AlexaFluor555

// ============================================================
// Digital Microfluidic Immunocytochemistry in Single Cells
// (DISC)
// Ng, A.H.C., Chamberlain, M.D., Situ, H., Lee, V., Wheeler,
// A.R. Nature Communications 6:7513 (2015).
// DOI: 10.1038/ncomms8513
//
// Protocol summary: DMF automates all steps for adherent cell
// culture, serum starvation, PDGF-BB ligand stimulation, and
// immunocytochemistry (ICC) on NIH-3T3 fibroblasts cultured in
// virtual microwells (VMs) on the patterned top plate of the
// DMF device. Protein phosphorylation (PDGFR Y857/Y1021 and
// Akt S473) is probed by dual-channel immunofluorescence.
//
// DEVICE GEOMETRY (from paper Methods):
//   Bottom plate: 80 actuation electrodes (2.2 x 2.2 mm),
//     interdigitated borders (140 um sinusoids), 30-80 um gaps.
//   Top plate: 8 hydrophilic ITO spots (1.75 mm diameter,
//     4.4 mm pitch) formed by Teflon-AF lift-off.
//   Spacer: double-sided tape, ~180 um gap.
//   Unit droplet volume: ~900 nL; VM volume: ~400 nL.
//   Driving: 80-100 V_rms, 10 kHz sine wave.
//   Reagent exchange uses passive dispensing (hydrophobic-
//     hydrophilic interaction at ITO spots). One exchange
//     displaces ~93% of VM contents; two exchanges >99%.
//   Reagent exchange time: ~1 s between successive droplets.
//
// CELL SEEDING (paper Methods - "DMF cell culture"):
//   Cells suspended in CultureMedia at 500,000 cells/mL.
//   3 x 900 nL (= 2.7 uL) passively dispensed per VM spot.
//   Device inverted; cells settle and adhere for 24 h at 37 C.
//
// ICC PROTOCOL - 11 STEPS (paper Methods):
//   1.  Starvation:  6 x 900 nL StarvedMedia; 24 h at 37 C.
//   2.  Serum-free rinse: 6 x 900 nL SerumFreeMedia.
//   3.  Stimulation: 2 x 900 nL PDGF-BB (conc/time varies).
//   4.  Fixation:    3 x 900 nL 4% PFA; 10 min.
//   5.  Wash:        6 x 900 nL WashBuffer1.
//   6.  Permeabilisation: 3 x 900 nL 0.2% Tween-20; 10 min.
//   7.  Wash:        9 x 900 nL WashBuffer2.
//   8.  Blocking:    3 x 900 nL BlockingSolution; 60 min.
//   9.  1- antibody: 3 x 900 nL; overnight at 4 C (= 720 min).
//   10. Wash:        6 x 900 nL WashBuffer2.
//   11. 2- antibody: 3 x 900 nL; 2 h at RT.
//   Top plate removed, rinsed, dried, scanned on microarray
//   scanner. CellProfiler used for single-cell image analysis.
//
// NOTE ON PASSIVE DISPENSING ABSTRACTION:
//   All multi-unit passive dispense steps (e.g., 6 x 900 nL)
//   are modelled as single `dispense N units` calls. The
//   BioScript compiler treats `N units` as a volume scalar;
//   it does not generate array elements here, which is correct
//   because each VM receives the full merged volume, not N
//   independent droplets. All mixing steps merge successive
//   passive-dispense deliveries at the VM site.
//
// NOTE ON CONCURRENT VMs:
//   The DMF device supports 8 VMs on the top plate. The paper
//   runs 3-4 VMs per condition on different days. BioScript
//   does not support spatial parallelism natively; this file
//   encodes a single representative VM. For multi-VM runs,
//   replicate this instruction block or use a loop construct
//   if supported by the target compiler backend.
//
// NOTE ON TIME-RESOLVED PULSE EXPERIMENTS (Fig. 6):
//   The encoded protocol (BB1-BB9) reflects the dose-response
//   validation experiment (Fig. 3b/3c): 2 min PDGFR stimulation
//   and 5 min Akt stimulation (the representative use case).
//   For pulse experiments, only the stimulation duration and
//   the ligand wash-away step in BB1 change. The double-bolus
//   time series (Fig. 5b) would require a second dispense of
//   PDGF-BB at t=90 s with a second stimulationMix variable.
//   These variants are noted in-line but not separately encoded
//   to keep the CFG tractable for the lilott8/BioScript
//   compiler (which does not support nested conditionals or
//   timer-parameterised loops).
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- device setup, cell seeding,
//                             starvation, ICC steps 1-3
//                             (up to and including fixation)
//   BB2  stimulusPass      -- stimulusSignal > 0: PDGFR
//                             phosphorylation detected;
//                             dispose fixed cells
//   BB3  stimulusFail      -- stimulusSignal <= 0: no receptor
//                             phosphorylation signal; drain
//   BB4  stimulusJoin      -- join: Akt downstream branch begins
//   BB5  aktPass           -- aktSignal > 0: Akt S473
//                             phosphorylation detected; dispose
//   BB6  aktFail           -- aktSignal <= 0: no Akt signal;
//                             drain
//   BB7  aktJoin           -- join: secondary ICC steps begin
//   BB8  immunoPass        -- immunoSignal > 0: dual-channel
//                             ICC valid; dispose stained plate
//   BB9  immunoFail        -- immunoSignal <= 0: ICC failed;
//                             drain stained plate
//   BB10 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CELL SEEDING: Dispense cells in CultureMedia onto VM spots.
//   Paper M&M: 3 x 900 nL = 2.7 uL; 500,000 cells/mL.
//   Device inverted; 24 h at 37 C for adhesion.
//   `mix` abstracts passive dispensing flow across ITO spot
//   followed by sub-droplet VM formation (Supplementary Fig. 1).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cellSuspension   = dispense 3 units of NIH3T3_Cells
cultureDrop      = dispense 3 units of CultureMedia
seededVM         = mix cellSuspension with cultureDrop for 5s

// 24 h adhesion at 37 C in humidified chamber (= 1440 min).
heat seededVM at 37c for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1 - STARVATION: 6 x 900 nL StarvedMedia; 24 h at 37 C.
//   StarvedMedia: DMEM + 0.5% serum (CS or FBS) + 0.05% F-68
//                 + 100 U/mL pen G + 100 ug/mL strep.
//   Reduces background PDGFR and Akt phosphorylation to basal
//   level before stimulation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

starvedDrop      = dispense 6 units of StarvedMedia
starvedVM        = mix seededVM with starvedDrop for 5s

// 24 h starvation at 37 C (= 1440 min).
heat starvedVM at 37c for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2 - SERUM-FREE RINSE: 6 x 900 nL SerumFreeMedia.
//   SerumFreeMedia: DMEM + 0.05% F-68 + antibiotics.
//   Two passive-dispense exchanges displace >99% of starving
//   media from the VM (Fig. 2b-d). Encoded as single merge.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

serumFreeDrop    = dispense 6 units of SeumFreeMedia
rinsedVM         = mix starvedVM with serumFreeDrop for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3 - STIMULATION: 2 x 900 nL PDGF-BB in SerumFreeMedia.
//   Dose: paper validates 0 - 200 ng/mL range; 50 ng/mL used
//         for time-series (Fig. 5a) and cell heterogeneity
//         (Fig. 4); 3.125 ng/mL for pulse experiments (Fig. 6).
//   Duration: 2 min for PDGFR phosphorylation; 5 min for Akt.
//             Here encoded as 2 min (PDGFR validation arm).
//   For pulse experiments: a second wash droplet (SerumFreeMedia)
//   is dispensed after the desired pulse duration to wash away
//   the ligand before fixation (Supplementary Movie 2).
//   Switching time between droplets: ~1 s (Fig. 2a).
//
//   NOTE: Shear stress from DMF droplet movement is ~0.5 dyn/cm^2
//   (Supplementary Note 1), below the 1 dyn/cm^2 threshold for
//   flow-mediated Akt/Erk signalling. Tested explicitly with 75
//   back-and-forth droplet movements: P=0.7188, no difference
//   from undisturbed cells (Supplementary Fig. 8).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ligandDrop       = dispense 2 units of PDGFBB_Ligand
stimulatedVM     = mix rinsedVM with ligandDrop for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4 - FIXATION: 3 x 900 nL 4% PFA + 0.05% F-68; 10 min.
//   Immediately follows stimulation (within ~1 s reagent swap).
//   Fixation arrests signalling state at the exact time point.
//   In time-series experiments, fixation is staggered across
//   VMs so all wells are fixed simultaneously (paper M&M).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pfaDrop          = dispense 3 units of Paraformaldehyde
fixedVM          = mix stimulatedVM with pfaDrop for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5 - WASH: 6 x 900 nL WashBuffer1 (0.05% F-68 in DPBS).
//   Removes fixative before permeabilisation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash1Drop        = dispense 6 units of WashBuffer1
washedVM1        = mix fixedVM with wash1Drop for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6 - PERMEABILISATION: 3 x 900 nL 0.2% Tween-20; 10 min.
//   Opens cell membranes for intracellular antibody access.
//   Required for pAkt S473 (cytoplasmic/membrane) detection.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tween20Drop      = dispense 3 units of Tween20
permeabilisedVM  = mix washedVM1 with tween20Drop for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7 - WASH: 9 x 900 nL WashBuffer2 (0.05% Brij 35 in
//   DPBS). Extended wash to remove Tween-20 completely.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash2Drop        = dispense 9 units of WashBuffer2
washedVM2        = mix permeabilisedVM with wash2Drop for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8 - BLOCKING: 3 x 900 nL BlockingSolution; 60 min.
//   BlockingSolution: 1% non-fat dried milk + 0.05% Brij 35
//   in DPBS. Reduces non-specific antibody binding.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

blockDrop        = dispense 3 units of BlockingSolution
blockedVM        = mix washedVM2 with blockDrop for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9 - PRIMARY ANTIBODY: 3 x 900 nL; overnight at 4 C.
//   For PDGFR phosphorylation (Y857 arm - Fig. 3b):
//     pan PDGFR-b Mouse mAb (1:50, CST sc-19995)   -> Cy5 ch.
//     p-PDGFR-b Y857 Rabbit pAb (1:200, SCB sc-12907-R) -> Cy3.
//   For Akt phosphorylation (S473 arm - Fig. 3c):
//     pan Akt Mouse mAb (1:50, CST 2920S)           -> Cy5 ch.
//     p-Akt S473 Rabbit mAb (1:200, CST 4060P)      -> Cy3 ch.
//   Here encoded as PDGFR Y857 + Akt dual-target arm.
//   Overnight = 720 min; incubation at 4 C.
//
//   NOTE ON DUAL PRIMARY ANTIBODY MIX: The two primaries are
//   pre-mixed in BlockingSolution off-chip before loading into
//   the DMF reservoir. BioScript cannot express off-chip mixing
//   of manifested reagents; the two manifest entries are merged
//   here as a single `mix` before the blocking step application.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primary_PDGFR    = dispense 3 units of PrimaryAntibody_PDGFR
primary_pY857    = dispense 3 units of PrimaryAntibody_pPDGFR_Y857
primaryMix       = mix primary_PDGFR with primary_pY857 for 5s

primary_Akt      = dispense 3 units of PrimaryAntibody_Akt
primary_pS473    = dispense 3 units of PrimaryAntibody_pAkt_S473
primaryMix_Akt   = mix primary_Akt with primary_pS473 for 5s

combinedPrimary  = mix primaryMix with primaryMix_Akt for 5s
primaryStainedVM = mix blockedVM with combinedPrimary for 720m

// Overnight incubation at 4 C (= 720 min).
heat primaryStainedVM at 4c for 720m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10 - WASH: 6 x 900 nL WashBuffer2. Removes unbound
//   primary antibodies.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

wash3Drop        = dispense 6 units of WashBuffer2
washedVM3        = mix primaryStainedVM with wash3Drop for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11 - SECONDARY ANTIBODY: 3 x 900 nL; 2 h at RT.
//   Anti-Mouse IgG Alexa Fluor 647 (Fab2, 1:500, CST 4410S)
//     -> detects pan-PDGFR and pan-Akt (total protein, Cy5 ch.)
//   Anti-Rabbit IgG Alexa Fluor 555 (Fab2, 1:500, CST 4413S)
//     -> detects p-PDGFR Y857 and p-Akt S473 (Cy3 ch.)
//   Pre-mixed in BlockingSolution off-chip. Encoded as merge.
//   2 h at room temperature (25 C = 120 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

secondary_647    = dispense 3 units of SecondaryAntibody_AlexaFluor647
secondary_555    = dispense 3 units of SecondaryAntibody_AlexaFluor555
secondaryMix     = mix secondary_647 with secondary_555 for 5s

secondaryStained = mix washedVM3 with secondaryMix for 120m

// 2 h secondary antibody incubation at RT (25 C = 120 min).
heat secondaryStained at 25c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// DETECTION - PDGFR phosphorylation QC:
//   phosphorylationDetection abstracts off-chip microarray
//   scanner readout (Axon GenePix 4000B; 532 nm and 635 nm
//   lasers; 5 um resolution; PMT 500 V). CellProfiler 2.0
//   pipeline identifies single cells (15-100 um diameter,
//   Otsu Global thresholding) and computes fold-change ratio:
//   (Cy3 phospho-channel intensity) / (Cy5 total-protein
//   intensity), normalised to no-stimulation control on same
//   device. Signal > 1.0 (fold change) = phosphorylation above
//   basal level. QC gate uses bulk-average signal across VM.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stimulusSignal   = detect phosphorylationDetection on secondaryStained for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: PDGFR phosphorylation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): stimulusSignal > 0 -> receptor phosphorylation
//             above basal level detected; dispose stained VM.
// Fail (BB3): stimulusSignal <= 0 -> no detectable PDGFR
//             phosphorylation; drain (reagent failure or
//             no stimulation).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (stimulusJoin).
// ============================================================

if (stimulusSignal > 0) {
    dispose secondaryStained
} else {
    drain secondaryStained
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: stimulusJoin
// Dispose PDGFR QC signal. Control falls into downstream
// Akt phosphorylation branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose stimulusSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// AKT PHOSPHORYLATION ARM (Fig. 3c / Fig. 4 / Fig. 6b):
//   Separate VM seeded identically to the PDGFR arm above.
//   Stimulation: 5 min (vs 2 min for PDGFR) as per paper M&M.
//   Staining uses Akt / p-Akt S473 primary pair (see Step 9).
//
//   NOTE: In the paper's physical experiment, the Akt and
//   PDGFR arms run in parallel VMs on the same device. In this
//   BioScript encoding they are sequential (BioScript has no
//   native spatial parallelism for distinct VM populations).
//   The Akt VM re-runs the full ICC pipeline with modified
//   stimulation duration (5 min). Only the stimulation and
//   detection steps differ; the antibody panel is Akt-specific.
//
//   For the heterogeneity / hyperactive-responder analysis
//   (Fig. 4), stimulation is 0-7 min with 50 ng/mL PDGF-BB.
//   For the pulse experiments (Fig. 6b), stimulation is 3-40 s
//   followed by a ligand-free wash before fixation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// -- Akt arm: seeding and starvation (identical to PDGFR arm) --

aktCellSusp      = dispense 3 units of NIH3T3_Cells
aktCultureDrop   = dispense 3 units of CultureMedia
aktSeededVM      = mix aktCellSusp with aktCultureDrop for 5s
heat aktSeededVM at 37c for 1440m

aktStarvedDrop   = dispense 6 units of StarvedMedia
aktStarvedVM     = mix aktSeededVM with aktStarvedDrop for 5s
heat aktStarvedVM at 37c for 1440m

aktRinseDrop     = dispense 6 units of SeumFreeMedia
aktRinsedVM      = mix aktStarvedVM with aktRinseDrop for 5s

// -- Akt arm: STEP 3 - Stimulation: 5 min (vs 2 min for PDGFR) --
aktLigandDrop    = dispense 2 units of PDGFBB_Ligand
aktStimulated    = mix aktRinsedVM with aktLigandDrop for 5m

// -- Akt arm: STEP 4 - Fixation --
aktPfaDrop       = dispense 3 units of Paraformaldehyde
aktFixedVM       = mix aktStimulated with aktPfaDrop for 10m

// -- Akt arm: STEP 5 - Wash --
aktWash1         = dispense 6 units of WashBuffer1
aktWashedVM1     = mix aktFixedVM with aktWash1 for 5s

// -- Akt arm: STEP 6 - Permeabilisation --
aktTween20       = dispense 3 units of Tween20
aktPermVM        = mix aktWashedVM1 with aktTween20 for 10m

// -- Akt arm: STEP 7 - Wash --
aktWash2         = dispense 9 units of WashBuffer2
aktWashedVM2     = mix aktPermVM with aktWash2 for 5s

// -- Akt arm: STEP 8 - Blocking --
aktBlockDrop     = dispense 3 units of BlockingSolution
aktBlockedVM     = mix aktWashedVM2 with aktBlockDrop for 60m

// -- Akt arm: STEP 9 - Primary antibody (Akt-specific panel) --
aktPrimary_Akt   = dispense 3 units of PrimaryAntibody_Akt
aktPrimary_pS473 = dispense 3 units of PrimaryAntibody_pAkt_S473
aktPrimaryMix    = mix aktPrimary_Akt with aktPrimary_pS473 for 5s
aktPrimStained   = mix aktBlockedVM with aktPrimaryMix for 720m
heat aktPrimStained at 4c for 720m

// -- Akt arm: STEP 10 - Wash --
aktWash3         = dispense 6 units of WashBuffer2
aktWashedVM3     = mix aktPrimStained with aktWash3 for 5s

// -- Akt arm: STEP 11 - Secondary antibody --
aktSec647        = dispense 3 units of SecondaryAntibody_AlexaFluor647
aktSec555        = dispense 3 units of SecondaryAntibody_AlexaFluor555
aktSecondaryMix  = mix aktSec647 with aktSec555 for 5s
aktSecStained    = mix aktWashedVM3 with aktSecondaryMix for 120m
heat aktSecStained at 25c for 120m

// Detection: Akt S473 phosphorylation (Cy3/Cy5 dual channel).
aktSignal        = detect phosphorylationDetection on aktSecStained for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Akt S473 phosphorylation QC gate
// Pass (BB5): aktSignal > 0 -> Akt phosphorylation above basal;
//             dispose stained VM.
// Fail (BB6): aktSignal <= 0 -> no Akt activation detected;
//             drain (stimulation below commitment threshold or
//             reagent failure).
// Both branches converge at BB7 (aktJoin).
//
// Biological note: paper shows Akt response is amplified
// relative to PDGFR - at 3.125 ng/mL PDGF, ~22% receptor
// phosphorylation drives >70% Akt activation. A 10 s pulse
// is sufficient to commit >32% of cells to Akt activation
// (Fig. 6b). Akt deactivation is observed if 3 s pulse cells
// are evaluated at 5 min vs 3-4 min (Fig. 6c), consistent
// with enzymatic noise-filtering.
// ============================================================

if (aktSignal > 0) {
    dispose aktSecStained
} else {
    drain aktSecStained
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: aktJoin
// Dispose Akt QC signal. Control falls into final cell
// viability / morphology QC branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose aktSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// FINAL QC - CELL MORPHOLOGY / VIABILITY DETECTION:
//   cellViabilityDetection abstracts the CellProfiler post-
//   scan QC step in which cells are filtered by size
//   (15-100 um diameter), shape (eccentricity, form factor),
//   and staining quality. This is not a staining step; it is
//   a computational gate on the acquired microarray images.
//   Signal > 0: sufficient cells identified per VM (>=150
//   cells at 500,000 cells/mL) with valid signal-to-background
//   ratio (>5x primary vs secondary-only control).
//
//   The cellViabilityDetection module also captures the
//   hyperactive-responder sub-population analysis (Fig. 4):
//   cells are classified as hyperactive if p-Akt fold change
//   exceeds Q3 + 1.5 * IQR (outlier threshold in JMP 10).
//   Hyperactive cells show elongated morphology (higher
//   eccentricity, lower form factor) and increased neighbour
//   proximity relative to normal cells (Supplementary Fig. 13).
//
//   NOTE ON QC DROPLET DESIGN:
//   secondaryStained and aktSecStained are consumed (disposed
//   or drained) in the BB2/BB3 and BB5/BB6 gate branches
//   above. The BioScript SSA form would version them as [2]
//   if referenced again here, producing undefined-variable
//   errors in the IR. The fix is a dedicated QC droplet:
//   a fresh aliquot of WashBuffer2 is dispensed as a carrier
//   for the cellViabilityDetection module call. In the
//   physical experiment, this gate is purely computational
//   (CellProfiler runs on the already-acquired microarray
//   scan images); the fluid operand is a BioScript
//   requirement for the detect statement, not a wet-lab step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Fresh QC carrier droplet -- avoids SSA version-2 conflict.
qcCarrier        = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer2
immunoSignal     = detect cellViabilityDetection on qcCarrier for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Cell identification / ICC quality QC gate
// Pass (BB8): immunoSignal > 0 -> valid cell count and
//             signal-to-background ratio; dispose stained plate.
// Fail (BB9): immunoSignal <= 0 -> insufficient cells or
//             antibody staining failure; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (immunoSignal > 0) {
    dispose qcCarrier
} else {
    drain qcCarrier
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose the ICC QC signal droplet.
// Experiment ends; top plate removed for microarray scanner
// analysis and CellProfiler single-cell quantification.
// ============================================================

dispose immunoSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
